===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|colour}}, {{m|enm|color}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|colur}}, from {{der|en|fro|colour}}, {{m|fro|color}}, from {{der|en|la|color}}.

Displaced {{noncog|en|blee}}, {{noncog|enm|blee|t=color}}, from {{noncog|ang|blēo}}. Also partially replaced {{cog|ang|hīew||color}} and its descendants ({{cog|en|hue}}), which is less often used in this sense. {{doublet|en|couleur}}.

The spelling ''color'' was popularized in modern American English by Webster, to match the spelling of the word's Latin etymon{{,}} and make all American spellings of the derivatives consistent (''colorimeter'',  ''coloration'', ''colorize'', ''colorless'', etc).

